chart code :  ```python
import plotly.express as px
import pandas as pd

# Drop rows with missing values in 'ProductNumber' or 'ProductColor'
df = df.dropna(subset=['ProductNumber', 'ProductColor'])
df = df[~df['ProductNumber'].isin([''])]
df = df[~df['ProductColor'].isin([''])]


# Convert ProductNumber to numeric, handling non-numeric values
try:
    df['ProductNumber'] = pd.to_numeric(df['ProductNumber'], errors='coerce')
    df = df.dropna(subset=['ProductNumber'])
except (ValueError, TypeError):
    pass


fig = px.line(df, 
              x='ProductNumber', 
              y='ProductColor', 
              color='ProductColor',
              title='Line Chart for Each Product Color')
fig.show()

```
Query
sql query: ```sql
-- SSMS Query Start
SELECT
    AdventureWorks2022.Production.Product.Name,
    YEAR(AdventureWorks2022.Sales.SalesOrderDetail.ModifiedDate) AS SalesYear,
    SUM(AdventureWorks2022.Sales.SalesOrderDetail.LineTotal) AS TotalSales
FROM
    AdventureWorks2022.Production.Product
INNER JOIN
    AdventureWorks2022.Sales.SalesOrderDetail ON AdventureWorks2022.Production.Product.ProductID = AdventureWorks2022.Sales.SalesOrderDetail.ProductID
GROUP BY
    AdventureWorks2022.Production.Product.Name,
    YEAR(AdventureWorks2022.Sales.SalesOrderDetail.ModifiedDate)
ORDER BY
    AdventureWorks2022.Production.Product.Name,
    SalesYear;
```
