df = df[~df['Q4Sales'].isin([''])]


fig = px.bar(df, x='Month', y=['Q3Sales', 'Q4Sales'], barmode='group')
fig.show()

```
chart code :  ```python
import plotly.express as px
import pandas as pd

# Assuming df is already defined and populated

# Drop rows with NaN/blank values in required columns before plotting
df = df.dropna(subset=['Month', 'Q3Sales', 'Q4Sales'])

fig = px.bar(df, x='Month', y=['Q3Sales', 'Q4Sales'], barmode='group')
fig.show()

